# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and adjust. Every EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable is INLINED into the JS
# bundle at build time — only ever put public configuration here, never a secret or API key.
# (No AI/Anthropic key belongs here or anywhere in this app: every AI call goes through the backend.)

# Base URL of the existing ASP.NET Core API, including the /api/v1 prefix.
#
#  - iOS simulator / web preview (`npx expo start --web`) on the same machine as the API:
#      http://localhost:5080/api/v1
#  - Android emulator: the emulator's alias for the host machine's loopback:
#      http://10.0.2.2:5080/api/v1
#  - Physical device (Expo Go / dev build) on the same Wi-Fi as the API host: use the host's LAN IP,
#    e.g. http://192.168.1.20:5080/api/v1 — `localhost` on a phone is the phone itself. The API
#    must also listen on that interface (e.g. `ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://0.0.0.0:5080`).
#
# Web preview only: the API's CORS policy must allow the Expo web dev-server origin, e.g. start the
# API with `Cors__AllowedOrigins__0=http://localhost:8081`. Native apps are not subject to CORS.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5080/api/v1
